 repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-49\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-50\"\n  }\n ]\n}\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"spec\" kind=\"spec\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"assumptions\": [\n  \"If a driver records actions offline and their account is disabled or removed before synchronization, should those queued actions be accepted into the shared record? → assumed: No; online only.\",\n  \"Staff sign in through Meridian Microsoft accounts; customers use email/password, an emailed one-time code, and an emailed reset link, as specified in US-001; ASM-23's no-social/no-SSO constraint applies to customer sign-in, while the one-time code remains required.\",\n  \"The web app presents access, persistence, revocation, and workflow outcomes returned by the separate API; API authorization and data isolation are not asserted by UI requirements.\",\n  \"For temperature-history gaps, the web app shows the stock status returned by the API, does not infer or set a stock status, and shows no charge to an unobserved temperature tier; the API-side gap disposition is not specified by this web requirement.\",\n  \"Warehouse-local time governs cutoff, working-day, holiday, delivery-date, and route rules; dates and times are displayed in the user's local zone with the warehouse zone identified.\",\n  \"Numeric policy values stated in the drafts include a 15-minute silence interval, two-minute alert target, 25% budget warning, three consecutive in-band readings, and 30-day expiry restriction; server calculations and timing are API-side.\",\n  \"Logger gateway and inbound exports use the supplier's documented interface and file format; gateway ingestion is API-side. The logger export is separate from receipt-evidence files; separate evidence uploads, if used, are images or PDFs up to 10 MB each and are kept in cloud storage. The supported format contract needs confirmation.\",\n  \"Supported browsers are the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox; WCAG 2.1 AA applies to main flows.\",\n  \"The source request ends during US-009; driver behavior is limited to stated intent spans and Q-3/Q-4 decisions, with no unstated behavior inferred.\",\n  \"Recall responses record quantity and disposition per affected delivery, reconciling located, used, returned, disposed of, or otherwise accounted-for quantities; supporting documents are not required.\",\n  \"Planning volumes are up to 1,000 users and 100,000 records in the first year plus 5,000 reporting devices; backend capacity is API-side.\",\n  \"One minimum shelf-life value is set per customer organisation; customers and Dispatchers cannot set it per order.\",\n  \"When readings are missing, do not charge an assumed temperature tier automatically; the web app shows the gap, review status, and stock status returned by the API.\",\n  \"Treat on-hand as a total and show non-overlapping quantities for available, allocated, quarantined, On Hold, Rejected, Recalled, and Expired stock.\",\n  \"Keep the stated numeric policy values fixed: 15-minute silence, two-minute alert target, 25% remaining-budget alert, three consecutive in-band readings, and 30-day expiry restriction.\",\n  \"A System Administrator sets one minimum remaining shelf-life value per customer organisation; Dispatchers and customers cannot change it per order.\",\n  \"Use the serving warehouse's configured local time zone for its cut-off, working-day, and route rules; display dates and times in the user's local zone with the warehouse zone identified.\",\n  \"No existing spreadsheet or operational data is migrated; the system starts empty with seed data for setup.\",\n  \"Use the supplier gateway's existing documented batch API; Meridian provides interface documentation, credentials, and sample payloads.\",\n  \"Alerts are sent by email from fixed templates; no SMS or push notifications.\",\n  \"Who created and last changed each record, and when, are retained; no full audit trail is required.\",\n  \"Provide on-screen lists with filters and CSV export; no custom report builder is required.\",\n  \"The latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox are supported.\",\n  \"WCAG 2.1 AA applies to the main flows.\",\n  \"For each affected delivery, record the customer's response, quantity, and stated disposition; accept the response as accounted for without supporting documents.\",\n  \"Support up to 1,000 users and 100,000 records in the first year in addition to 5,000 reporting devices.\",\n  \"If a driver records actions offline and their account is disabled before those actions synchronize, queued actions are not accepted into the shared record.\",\n  \"When a logger or sensor has a reading gap, do not charge an assumed temperature tier automatically; flag the gap for quality review and show the stock status returned by the API.\",\n  \"A customer recall response reconciles each quantity as located, used, returned, disposed of, or otherwise accounted for.\",\n  \"No existing paper-record or spreadsheet information is migrated; the system starts empty with seed data for setup.\",\n  \"Use Meridian's existing supplier gateway and documented interface, and accept the supplier's documented inbound logger export format.\",\n  \"Excursion and route alerts use email only from fixed templates; no SMS or push.\",\n  \"Customer users use email and password, an emailed one-time code, and an emailed reset link; customer social sign-in and customer SSO are excluded. Staff use Meridian Microsoft accounts.\",\n  \"Who created and last changed each record, and when, are retained; no full audit trail is required.\",\n  \"The latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox are supported.\",\n  \"WCAG 2.1 AA applies to the main flows.\",\n  \"Use the configured local time zone of the serving warehouse for order cut-offs, working days, delivery dates, and route times.\",\n  \"Support up to 1,000 users and 100,000 records in the first year in addition to 5,000 reporting devices.\"\n ],\n \"nfrs\": [\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-1\",\n   \"metric\": \"At viewport widths 320, 768, and 1280/1440 CSS pixels, zero horizontal overflow; phone interactive targets are at least 44 × 44 CSS pixels.\",\n   \"text\": \"Every portal page reflows for phone, tablet, and desktop browser widths, with touch-sized controls on narrow layouts.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-2\",\n   \"metric\": \"100% of the agreed main-flow screens pass WCAG 2.1 AA checks; zero unmet applicable success criteria in audited main flows.\",\n   \"text\": \"Main staff, customer, and driver web flows conform to WCAG 2.1 Level AA.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-3\",\n   \"metric\": \"100% of agreed main-flow UI test cases pass on the latest two versions of each of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox.\",\n   \"text\": \"The responsive portals support the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-4\",\n   \"metric\": \"1,000 users, 100,000 records in the first year, and data from 5,000 devices reporting at once.\",\n   \"text\": \"The web portal supports the stated first-year user and record volume and displays data from the stated simultaneous device volume.\"\n  }\n ],\n \"outOfScope\": [\n  \"API-side durable persistence, server-side role and organisation enforcement, session revocation, server-side validation and workflow transitions, stock and allocation concurrency/invariants, policy calculations, expiry processing, recall blocking, and database-level audit retention; web requirements cover presentation of API responses.\",\n  \"API-side supplier-gateway ingestion, reading deduplication and reordering, sensor-scale ingestion and processing, silence and excursion detection, stability-budget recalculation, hold placement, and alert timing; web requirements cover returned histories, statuses, and alerts.\",\n  \"API-side email alert and password-reset or one-time-code delivery. SMS and native push channels are excluded; where notification is needed in the web product, it is represented by in-app notice or email as specified by the source requirements.\",\n  \"Historical spreadsheet or paper-record import is excluded; setup uses seed data.\",\n  \"A full immutable audit trail beyond returned creator and last-change identity and timestamps is excluded.\",\n  \"A custom report builder is excluded.\",\n  \"Native iOS/Android binaries and app-store publication are excluded; requested driver functions are delivered in the responsive web app.\"\n ],\n \"requirements\": [\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A signed-in staff or customer user has portal access\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-1.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows links to the modules permitted for that user, including applicable stock, order, delivery, temperature, quality, and recall pages\",\n     \"when\": \"the user opens portal navigation\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A user opens an available workflow at phone, tablet, and desktop viewport widths\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-1.2\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen content has no horizontal overflow and phone controls have touch targets of at least 44 by 44 CSS pixels\",\n     \"when\": \"the page is rendered\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall provide role-oriented portal pages and navigation for stock, orders, deliveries, temperature monitoring, quality decisions, and recalls on phone, tablet, and desktop browser widths.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-1\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"I-2\",\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"I-4\",\n    \"I-15\",\n    \"ASM-13\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 0.6666666666666666\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A staff user opens staff sign-in\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the Meridian Microsoft sign-in option and no external staff-account form\",\n     \"when\": \"the user selects the staff sign-in flow\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API returns a one-time-code challenge after a customer submits email and password\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.2\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows a code-entry field, no customer social sign-in or single-sign-on option, and no customer account content before a successful code response\",\n     \"when\": \"the customer submits the credentials\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A customer user requests a password reset\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.3\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the request contains the customer email address and the screen shows the reset-link-by-email confirmation returned by the API\",\n     \"when\": \"the reset request is submitted\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A disabled or removed account attempts online sign-in or access\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.4\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows an access-denied message and no protected page or record is displayed\",\n     \"when\": \"the API returns an access-denied response\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall provide staff authentication through Meridian Microsoft accounts and customer authentication using email and password followed by a one-time code, with reset links requested by email and no social sign-in or single-sign-on option for customer accounts.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-2\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-2\",\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"I-7\",\n    \"ASM-23\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API returns records for a staff member's assigned warehouses or a customer's organisation\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-3.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows only the returned records\",\n     \"when\": \"the user opens the corresponding list\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A Quality Manager or Auditor opens a warehouse-scoped list and the API returns all-warehouse records\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-3.2\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the returned records from all warehouses\",\n     \"when\": \"the list is displayed\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An Auditor opens a record page\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-3.3\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows record details without create, edit, or delete controls, and an API-refused write is shown as an error message\",\n     \"when\": \"the page renders\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A protected request is refused because the account or record is inaccessible\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-3.4\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows an access-ended or access-denied message and clears protected record fields\",\n     \"when\": \"the web app receives the refusal\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When a user opens portal views, the Meridian responsive web app shall show records and actions returned for that user's role, assigned warehouses, and customer organisation, present Auditor views as read-only, and clear protected data when the API refuses access.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-3\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-2\",\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"I-7\",\n    \"ASM-1\",\n    \"ASM-17\",\n    \"ASM-11\",\n    \"ASM-23\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A Customer Administrator opens user management for their organisation\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-4.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the invitation or removal status returned by the API\",\n     \"when\": \"the administrator submits an invitation or removal\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API refuses a user-management action, including an action for another organisation\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-4.2\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the returned error message and does not show the other organisation's user as changed\",\n     \"when\": \"the administrator submits the action\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall let a Customer Administrator invite and remove users through controls scoped to that administrator's customer organisation.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-4\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"I-7\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 0.6666666666666666\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A System Administrator searches by product name or code or opens a deactivated product\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-5.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows matching product records and identifies deactivated products as unavailable for ordering\",\n     \"when\": \"the API returns matching products and active states\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A System Administrator submits an incomplete profile or one with overlapping or gapped tiers\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-5.2\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the validation error returned by the API and does not show the product as saved\",\n     \"when\": \"the administrator attempts to save\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A System Administrator submits a valid profile with tiers, reason, and effective date\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-5.3\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the request includes the profile tiers, reason, and effective date and the screen shows the new profile version returned by the API\",\n     \"when\": \"the profile change is submitted\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A product has multiple profile versions\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-5.4\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen lists earlier versions with their returned values, reason, effective date, and creator where returned, and provides no edit controls for earlier versions\",\n     \"when\": \"a user opens profile history\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A System Administrator deactivates a product\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-5.5\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the product as deactivated\",\n     \"when\": \"the API returns the updated product status\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall let System Administrators list, search, view, deactivate, and maintain products and create versioned temperature profiles with storage bands, contiguous non-overlapping tiers, allowance or not-permitted designations, a reason, and an effective date, while keeping earlier versions read-only.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-5\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-8\",\n    \"I-10\",\n    \"ASM-4\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API returns a new effective profile version and recalculated values for stock still held from the effective date onward\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-6.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the new version's effective date and the returned budget and decision values\",\n     \"when\": \"a user opens the profile and affected stock views\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A profile effective date is backdated and the API returns recalculation results for stock remaining in Meridian inventory on or after that effective date\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-6.2\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the returned recalculated budget and decision values and current workflow status without displaying a superseded status as current\",\n     \"when\": \"a user opens the affected stock, order, box, or route view\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A System Administrator submits a profile change with a reason and effective date\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-6.3\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the new version, reason, effective date, and returned recalculated budget and decision values\",\n     \"when\": \"the API returns the updated profile and affected-stock results\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A backdated profile recalculation affects stock that is allocated, packed, or on a route and the API returns resulting allocation, box, or route statuses or action requirements\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-6.4\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the returned allocation, box, and route statuses and any returned action-required message or handover restriction\",\n     \"when\": \"an authorized user opens or refreshes the affected order, box, or route\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When a temperature-profile version takes effect, the Meridian responsive web app shall show the new version and API-returned recalculated budgets, decisions, and current statuses for stock in Meridian inventory on or after the effective date, including resulting order, box, and route statuses for affected allocated or packed stock.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-6\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-8\",\n    \"I-9\",\n    \"I-11\",\n    \"I-17\",\n    \"Q-8\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 0.6666666666666666\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A Warehouse Operator opens the receipt form\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-7.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows fields for product, lot number, expiry date, quantity, supplier, cold room, and shelf\",\n     \"when\": \"the form is displayed\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API accepts a receipt with an inbound logger file\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-7.2\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the receipt record, Quarantined status, submitted receipt details, and returned inbound readings and budget use when available\",\n     \"when\": \"the operator submits the receipt\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API refuses a receipt with an expired lot date or missing required field\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-7.3\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the returned error message beside the relevant field and no saved receipt is displayed\",\n     \"when\": \"the operator submits the receipt\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When a Warehouse Operator records a receipt, the Meridian responsive web app shall capture product, lot number, expiry date, quantity, supplier, and storage location and show returned quarantine status and inbound temperature information before a release decision.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-7\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-9\",\n    \"ASM-9\",\n    \"ASM-21\",\n    \"ASM-4\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A Warehouse Operator uploads an inbound logger file in the configured supplier interface format\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-8.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the request includes the uploaded logger file and the screen shows the returned inbound readings and budget use before release controls\",\n     \"when\": \"the receipt is submitted\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A Warehouse Operator uploads a logger file rejected by the API\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-8.2\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the returned file error message and no successful-upload indicator\",\n     \"when\": \"the upload response is displayed\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An operator uploads a separate receipt-evidence image or PDF larger than 10 MB or a separate receipt-evidence file that is not an image or PDF\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-8.3\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows a validation error and no saved receipt is displayed\",\n     \"when\": \"the operator attempts to submit the receipt\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall provide inbound logger-file upload and display returned temperature history and budget use, validate separate image or PDF receipt-evidence files, and accept logger exports in the supplier's documented format.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-8\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-5\",\n    \"I-8\",\n    \"I-9\",\n    \"ASM-8\",\n    \"ASM-9\",\n    \"ASM-21\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A quarantined receipt is opened by a Quality Officer\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-9.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows returned receipt data, temperature-budget use, and release decision controls\",\n     \"when\": \"the receipt review page renders\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A receipt is within 30 days of expiry on arrival or the API refuses release\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-9.2\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the reason returned by the API and does not display the stock as released\",\n     \"when\": \"a Quality Officer opens or submits the release decision\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A Quality Officer proposes a disposition for stock exposed to a not-permitted range\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-9.3\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the request includes the proposed disposition and reason and the screen shows the proposal awaiting a different Quality Manager's approval\",\n     \"when\": \"the proposal is submitted\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The proposing person attempts to approve, or a user without the Quality Manager role attempts approval\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-9.4\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the returned error message or disables the approval control and shows the decision as unapproved\",\n     \"when\": \"the approval is attempted\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A different Quality Manager approves or rejects a pending disposition\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-9.5\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the returned decision, decision-maker, and decision status\",\n     \"when\": \"the API returns the final decision\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When quality staff review a receipt or excursion, the Meridian responsive web app shall present available release or disposition actions and show decision states returned by the API, including separate proposal and approval steps for not-permitted-range dispositions.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-9\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-9\",\n    \"I-14\",\n    \"Q-1\",\n    \"Q-2\",\n    \"ASM-4\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 0.6666666666666666\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API returns on-hand and status quantities for a product, lot, and warehouse\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-10.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the on-hand total and each returned status quantity as a separate field or row, with the quantities summing to the on-hand count\",\n     \"when\": \"a user opens the stock view\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API returns stock rows for multiple lots or warehouses\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-10.2\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows only rows matching the selected filter values\",\n     \"when\": \"a user filters the stock list\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall show on-hand stock with mutually exclusive quantities for available, allocated, quarantined, On Hold, Rejected, Recalled, and Expired statuses, and show returned warehouse, lot, product, receipt, and location details.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-10\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"I-6\",\n    \"I-9\",\n    \"I-11\",\n    \"I-17\",\n    \"Q-7\",\n    \"ASM-3\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A received lot is divided into handling units with different temperature histories\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-11.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows separate rows or records with each unit's returned quantity, history, and budget values\",\n     \"when\": \"a user opens the lot's handling-unit view\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When portions of received stock have different temperature histories, the Meridian responsive web app shall show them as separate handling units with their returned quantity, history, and tier-budget use and remaining.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-11\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-6\",\n    \"I-8\",\n    \"I-9\",\n    \"I-13\",\n    \"I-14\",\n    \"Q-5\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A Warehouse Operator moves stock between shelves or cold rooms\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-12.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the request includes the source and destination and the screen shows the returned movement record with actor, time, and quantity fields\",\n     \"when\": \"the operator submits the move and opens its result\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall provide stock-movement forms and show the returned movement record with source and destination locations, quantity, actor, and time.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-12\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-9\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 0.3333333333333333\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A Customer Administrator opens address management\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-13.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the address list or status returned by the API\",\n     \"when\": \"the administrator adds, edits, or removes an address\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A System Administrator changes minimum remaining shelf life for a customer organisation\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-13.2\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the request includes the organisation-level value and the screen shows the saved value and response status returned by the API\",\n     \"when\": \"the change is submitted\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A customer user or Dispatcher opens an order form\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-13.3\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the organisation's minimum remaining shelf-life value without a control to change it per order\",\n     \"when\": \"the form renders\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall let Customer Administrators maintain their organisation's saved delivery addresses and let System Administrators set the organisation's minimum remaining shelf-life requirement, showing that value read-only to customer users and Dispatchers.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-13\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"I-10\",\n    \"I-11\",\n    \"Q-6\",\n    \"ASM-5\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A customer user opens the order form\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-14.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen provides fields for at least one product line, a quantity of at least one pack per line, a saved address, requested delivery date, and partial-or-complete delivery preference\",\n     \"when\": \"the form is displayed\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A customer enters a quantity below one pack or submits an order without a line\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-14.2\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows a field error and the request is not sent\",\n     \"when\": \"the customer submits the form\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API returns eligible delivery dates for the serving warehouse, based on its configured local time, cut-off, working days, and holidays\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-14.3\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows only returned eligible dates, applies the next-working-day rule for an order before cut-off and no-earlier-than-the-working-day-after-that rule for an order after cut-off, and identifies the warehouse time zone\",\n     \"when\": \"the customer opens the date selector before or after the configured cut-off\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A customer selects a deactivated product for an order\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-14.4\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows that the product cannot be ordered and provides no orderable quantity field\",\n     \"when\": \"the product status is returned\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A customer selects products, quantities, address, date, and fulfillment choice\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-14.5\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the complete order summary\",\n     \"when\": \"the customer reviews the order before submission\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall let customer users create orders with one or more product lines, pack quantities, an organisation-saved delivery address, an eligible delivery date, and a choice between delivery of available quantities and complete delivery only.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-14\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"I-10\",\n    \"ASM-5\",\n    \"ASM-6\",\n    \"ASM-27\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API returns an order with line quantities and a status before Packed\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-15.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows each line's allocated and outstanding quantities and customer change and cancel controls\",\n     \"when\": \"the customer opens the order\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API returns an order status of Packed or later\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-15.2\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the current status and no customer change or cancel controls\",\n     \"when\": \"the customer opens the order\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A cancellation or change is refused or accepted by the API\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-15.3\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the returned error or cancellation response, current status, updated quantities, and stock availability count when returned\",\n     \"when\": \"the customer submits the action or refreshes the order\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A customer submits an order more than once or retries after a network interruption\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-15.4\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the captured request uses the same submission key for the retry and the screen shows one returned order record\",\n     \"when\": \"the web app sends the submission or retry\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An order submission is pending\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-15.5\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen sends only one order-submission request\",\n     \"when\": \"the customer repeats the submission\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A Dispatcher opens an order in Packed or later status and the API returns cancellation as available\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-15.6\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the dispatcher cancellation control and the returned cancellation response or error message\",\n     \"when\": \"the Dispatcher opens the order or submits cancellation\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When customers view, change, or cancel an order, the Meridian responsive web app shall show order status and allocated and outstanding quantities per line, expose customer change and cancellation controls only before Packed, expose dispatcher cancellation controls when returned as available, and display API outcomes.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-15\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"I-10\",\n    \"I-11\",\n    \"Q-6\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An order line is allocated across lots\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-16.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows each returned lot, expiry date, allocated quantity, line split, and outstanding quantity separately\",\n     \"when\": \"a Dispatcher or customer opens allocation details\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A Dispatcher selects an alternative lot\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-16.2\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows a required reason field and the request includes the chosen lot and reason, while the screen shows the accepted allocation or returned refusal message\",\n     \"when\": \"the override form renders and is submitted\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API reports back order, complete-only status, or no suitable stock\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-16.3\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the returned allocation status and outstanding quantity\",\n     \"when\": \"the Dispatcher opens the order\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"Allocated stock becomes On Hold, Rejected, Recalled, or Expired\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-16.4\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the returned removed allocation, replacement allocation outcome, outstanding quantity, and dispatcher message or notification outcome when returned\",\n     \"when\": \"the order view refreshes\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"Stock allocated to an order is reported by the API as On Hold, Rejected, Recalled, or Expired after it has been packed or placed on a route\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-16.5\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the returned stock status, resulting allocation and box or route status, and any returned action-required message or handover restriction\",\n     \"when\": \"a user opens or refreshes the affected order, box, or route view\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall show order allocations by line and lot, including returned expiry dates and quantities, expose dispatcher lot-override controls with a required reason and API outcome, and show returned allocation and stock-status outcomes in order, box, and route views.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-16\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-10\",\n    \"I-11\",\n    \"I-12\",\n    \"I-15\",\n    \"I-17\",\n    \"ASM-5\",\n    \"Q-6\",\n    \"Q-7\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A Warehouse Operator opens the packing form\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-17.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen provides fields for box type, logger identifier, delivery stop, products, lots, and quantities\",\n     \"when\": \"the form renders\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The operator selects stock, a box type, and logger and submits the packing action\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-17.2\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the returned compatibility result or error message and does not show an unsuccessful box as sealed\",\n     \"when\": \"the API returns compatibility results or refuses an incompatible band, box type, missing logger, or already-associated logger\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A box is ready to be sealed and sealing succeeds\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-17.3\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows exactly one logger requirement and the returned seal time, operator, contents, quantities, and logger\",\n     \"when\": \"the operator opens the box record\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall let Warehouse Operators pack stock into shipper boxes by type, associate one logger with each box, and show compatibility, contents, and sealing details returned by the API.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-17\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-9\",\n    \"I-12\",\n    \"I-13\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A Dispatcher creates a route\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-18.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen provides fields for one vehicle, one driver, route date, at least one ordered stop, and planned arrival times\",\n     \"when\": \"the route form is displayed\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API refuses confirmation because a box exceeds its qualified duration after applying the configured safety margin, which defaults to 4 hours\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-18.2\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen shows the refused status,